# Error log maintenance

When an error is encountered and fixed during work in this repo, append an entry to [docs/errors.md](docs/errors.md).

## Requirements

1. Use the next `E-NNN` id (increment from the highest existing entry; start at `E-001`).
2. Put the new entry at the **top** of the Entries section (newest first).
3. Fill: Date, Area, Symptoms, Cause, Fix, Future notes.
4. Write Cause as the root cause, not a restatement of the symptom.
5. Future notes must be actionable (what to check, avoid, or automate next time).
6. Remove the `_No errors logged yet._` placeholder when adding the first entry.
7. Update the **Last updated** date in the doc header.
8. Do not invent entries for hypothetical errors; only log real failures that occurred.

## When to log

- Build / type / lint failures that blocked progress
- Runtime bugs and regressions
- Tooling / env / dependency issues
- Integration or demo breakages
- Wrong assumptions that wasted time once corrected

Skip trivial one-keystroke typos unless they reveal a recurring trap.
